RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
May 11, 2009
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne met on this date beginning at 6:00 p.m. in
Council Chambers.  Present were: MAYOR - Richard L. Kaysen; COUNCIL MEMBERS - Ms.
Ash, Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles, Ms. Case, Mr. Collins, Mr. Pierson, Mr. Spiker and Mr. Valdez.
Absent: Dr.  Rinne.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.

Also present: Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Barb Dorr, City Treasurer, and Dan White, City
Attorney.
Consent Agenda. (All agenda items listed with the designation of [CA] are considered to be
routine items by the governing body and will be enacted by one motion.  There will be no separate
discussion on these items unless a member of the governing body so requests and support by two
other members is received.  Any item removed from the Consent Agenda will be considered in its
normal sequence on the agenda.)  Upon request by Mr. Collins, and pursuant to support received by
Mr. Brown and Ms. Ash, agenda item #35(d) was removed from the Consent Agenda.  Mr. Collins
moved to approve remaining Consent Agenda items, seconded by Mr. Brown.  Mr. Spiker declared
a conflict of interest pertaining to Consent Agenda item #38 (a) and vacated Council Chambers.
Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present in Council Chambers.
Following announcement of the vote, Mr. Spiker returned to Council Chambers.
RECOGNITION OF THE 100TH ANNIVERSARY OF COMMUNITY SERVICE BY
THE CHEYENNE FIRE AND RESCUE DEPARTMENT.  Fire Chief Guy Cameron commented
on the celebration of the 100th anniversary of the Fire Department, recognizing those who have
supported the department over the years, including former Hook and Ladder companies, previous
Fire Department staff, citizens of Cheyenne who have supported the 5th and 6th penny sales tax
which helps fund the department, and current and former members of the governing body.  He
briefly reviewed the fire department’s history and services that have been provided.  In recognition
of support by current members of the governing body, Chief Cameron presented each member
present with a letter of appreciation and a commemorative coin. Mayor Kaysen expressed
appreciation and gratitude to past and present Fire Department staff.
 [CA]
MINUTES FROM REGULAR MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON APRIL 27,
2009.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
 [CA]
MINUTES FROM VOUCHERS MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON MAY 4,
2009.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
Mr. Collins moved to approve payment of vouchers as presented, seconded by Mr. Valdez.
Mr. Brown declared a conflict of interest (voucher payable to his business, Ameri-Tech HVAC
Services, $15,562.50) and vacated Council Chambers.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members
of the governing body present in Council Chambers.  Following announcement of the vote, Mr.
Brown returned to Council Chambers.
Mayor Kaysen opened a public hearing for the purpose of receiving comments and input to
determine whether compliance of annexation conditions required by Wyo. Stat. § 15-1-402 exists
```

